        <h2 id="overview">What is Semaglutide?</h2>
        <p>Semaglutide is a GLP-1 receptor agonist developed by Novo Nordisk. It mimics the naturally occurring GLP-1 hormone in your gut, but with a much longer duration of action. A single dose remains active in your body for approximately one week, making it far more potent and practical than the hormone your body produces on its own.</p>
        <p>First approved by the FDA in 2017 for type 2 diabetes (as Ozempic), semaglutide gained massive attention when higher-dose formulations showed dramatic weight loss results, leading to Wegovy's approval for weight management in 2021.</p>

